# The interpolation renderer: `40_format_vectors.ds` logs one line per spec,
# and the log text is compared, pinning [LGRA.2.9.6.10] and [LGRA.2.9.6.4]
# across the runtimes. No recording carries a log atom, so only `mercury
# diff` sees this. Each fact reaches a different rule:
#
#   1  the plain case: positive, short text, the epoch
#   2  negatives -- a negative `x` and `b` print the magnitude with `-`; `-0.0`
#      keeps its sign; a multi-byte String cut by precision and padded by code
#      points; one nanosecond before the epoch floors
#   3  the extremes -- min_int64 has no positive twin; a Float in scientific
#      form; the empty String; a fraction under `%f`
#   4  `f` rounds: 0.129 at two places is 0.13
assert V id=1 i=42 f=3.14159 s="kitchen" bl=true t=0
pump
assert V id=2 i=-7 f=-0.0 s="héllo" bl=false t=-1
pump
assert V id=3 i=-9223372036854775808 f=1e-05 s="" bl=true t=1234567890
pump
assert V id=4 i=255 f=0.129 s="abcdefghij" bl=false t=86399999999999
pump
